    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" caput="10" para="true">CAPUT X.</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Mista numeratione.</l>
    <l n="3" type="diagram" level="1">D. Mista nu-</l>
    <l n="4" type="diagram" level="1">meratio est aut</l>
    <l n="5" type="diagram" level="2">Accidentalis, &amp; est Reductio uel</l>
    <l n="6" type="diagram" level="3">Integrorum.</l>
    <l n="7" type="diagram" level="3">Mistorum.</l>
    <l n="8" type="diagram" level="2">Essentialis, cu-</l>
    <l n="9" type="diagram" level="2">ius Species duae</l>
    <l n="10" type="diagram" level="2">sunt</l>
    <l n="11" type="diagram" level="3">Prima</l>
    <l n="12" type="diagram" level="4">Additio.</l>
    <l n="13" type="diagram" level="4">Subductio.</l>
    <l n="14" type="diagram" level="3">Secunda</l>
    <l n="15" type="diagram" level="4">Multiplicatio.</l>
    <l n="16" type="diagram" level="4">Diuisio.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">HACTENVS de simplici nume-</l>
    <l n="18">ratione: superest Mista, in</l>
    <l n="19">qua dati numerandi</l>
    <l n="20">sunt in-</l>
    <l n="21">tegra cum partibus. Atque</l>
    <l n="22">haec quoque numeratio non</l>
    <l n="23">secus quàm partiu duplex est, Accidentalis,</l>
    <l n="24">praeter dictas reductiones, tum in-</l>
    <l n="25">tegrorum, tum mistorum reductione ad</l>
    <l n="26">Partes absoluitur.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The woodcut initial is an H, joined to the word "ACTENVS" as "HACTENVS". The diagram labels are read from the brace structure; the "D." before "Mista" is taken as a printed letter mark. "partiu" is printed as such, probably for partium. The left strip of the scan shows the edge of the neighbouring page, which is not transcribed.</notes>
